{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-torsion-leaf-minimum","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-torsion-leaf-minimum","kind":"remark","title":"q-Torsion leaves as energy minima","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-torsion-leaf"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","tags":["q-deformation","torsion","curvature"],"text":"q-torsion-leaf-minimum.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-torsion-leaf-minimum\"></a><p>A <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-torsion leaf <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L</code> is a local minimum of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lVert\\Omega_q\\rVert</code> restricted to the horizontal distribution. The Reeb-flow invariance forces the first variation of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lVert\\Omega_q|_L\\rVert</code> to vanish, situating <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L</code> inside a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-curvature well.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-torsion-leaf-minimum.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.27.1"}
